From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] grt: global_route -no_incremental frees the router once
 the routes are saved
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FastRoute keeps its nets, Steiner trees, per-edge route grids and grid
after global_route returns, for incremental routing: ORFS's global route
stage repairs and then reroutes the nets it changed. A flow that reroutes
nothing afterwards keeps them, on a large design many GB, through
everything that follows, write_db and timing among them.

global_route -no_incremental frees them once the routes are saved; the
routes, which parasitics estimation reads, stay, and the result is the
same. A later -start_incremental rebuilds the router from the routes, as
it does on a design read from odb. Graph2D::clear now also frees the
capacity per layer and the NDR nets per edge, which initCap3D allocates
again.

gcd_no_incremental routes gcd with -no_incremental, then incrementally,
and expects gcd's guides.

Carried in bazel-orfs for OpenROAD#12075, not upstreamed; retires with
the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
