diff --git a/src/grt/README.md b/src/grt/README.md
index 4641bf2440..3adc56dea1 100644
--- a/src/grt/README.md
+++ b/src/grt/README.md
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ global_route
     [-allow_congestion]
     [-snapshot_batched_width width]
     [-backing_file file]
+    [-no_incremental]
     [-verbose]
     [-start_incremental]
     [-end_incremental]
@@ -58,6 +59,7 @@ global_route
 | `-infinite_cap` | Enables "infinite" gcell capacity for testing purpose. NOTE: this is not recommended for production flows. |
 | `-snapshot_batched_width` | Set the semantic width of snapshot-batched routing (max batches per wave). The default is `0`, preserving the non-batched behavior. Set a positive integer to enable batched routing; allowed values are integers `[1, MAX_INT]`. Execution width still follows `set_thread_count`. NOTE: this is not recommended for production flows; it is intended for exploration and research projects. |
 | `-backing_file` | Back the routing grid (the 2D and 3D edges and the capacity per layer) with a file at this path instead of memory alone, so the kernel pages it to the file rather than to swap. The file is reserved for the whole grid when the grid is set up, which fails at once if the disk cannot hold it, and is removed as soon as it is created. The routes are the same as without it. |
+| `-no_incremental` | Free the router's own nets, Steiner trees and grid once the routes are saved, for a flow that does not reroute incrementally afterwards. The routes are the same; a later `-start_incremental` rebuilds the router from them. |
 
 ### Set Routing Layers
 
